00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:22,228
If he works for one of the seven
warlords, he'll get amnesty.

253
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:23,590
Tricky.

254
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:26,220
Hello there.

255
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:30,777
You're the famous vice-admiral who got
recruited in the World Military Draft,

256
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:31,690
aren't you?

257
00:16:32,580 --> 00:16:33,580
Fujitoro, was it?

258
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:36,797
They say you and Vice
Admiral Ryokyugyu are both

259
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:39,586
forces to be reckoned
with on the battlefield.

260
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,340
Sir, you flatter me.

261
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:44,080
You can spare me the humble act.

262
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:45,778
Then I'll be frank.

263
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:48,817
I'm having some trouble
unraveling the situation.

264
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:51,841
You see, I don't have much
experience as a Marine,

265
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:55,102
so I don't want to make
any baseless accusations.

266
00:16:55,540 --> 00:16:57,740
But it seems to me, as a warlord,

267
00:16:58,080 --> 00:17:02,277
you're doing some things that step
outside of your boundaries just a bit.

268
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:03,300
For example,

269
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:08,561
the fellow over there just referred to you
as Joker, a rather troubling implication.

270
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:14,317
If you want to dig into my past, you'd
better be willing to get your hands dirty.

271
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:17,635
because it'll take a mountain
of evidence to topple me.

272
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:19,426
Speaking of naughty warlords,

273
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:22,035
what's the Navy going to do about law?

274
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:32,297
You're referring to the news about his
alliance with the infamous pirate Straw Hat.

275
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:35,077
If the reports are true,
then I'm afraid he's guilty.

276
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:40,477
So tell me: law, is he simply
your subordinate or is he an ally?

277
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:46,817
And you're guilty—what comes
next depends on your answer.

278
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:48,617
If you betrayed your position.

279
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:52,994
position will have to arrest both you
and the Straw Hats for your crimes.

280
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:55,940
What kind of half-assed decision is that?

281
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:59,057
All he has to do is lie and
you let him go scot-free?

282
00:17:59,140 --> 00:18:00,980
My plan fell completely apart.

283
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,912
The Navy shows up and now I'm the target.

284
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:09,316
I can't let the team in
Dressrosa be affected by this.

285
00:18:09,480 --> 00:18:12,068
I'm going to have to
make a stand on my own.

286
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:14,680
Lying won't help. It's true!

287
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,857
The Straw Hats aren't working under me!

288
00:18:16,940 --> 00:18:18,705
We're equals in this alliance!

289
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:23,620
Just can't take the easy way, can you?

290
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,340
Well, that's it.

291
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:28,100
Your title is revoked.

292
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:31,202
But that might not be the
only headline tomorrow.

293
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:47,820
No way.

294
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:53,177
Meteor? That...

295
00:18:53,260 --> 00:18:54,480
that can't be right!

296
00:18:57,860 --> 00:19:01,200
That's a bit overkill, don't
you think? It's a meteor!

297
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,320
One more gazillion!

298
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:04,750
Go!

299
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:47,517
It's not here.

300
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:49,137
I can't see what I'm saying.

301
00:19:49,220 --> 00:19:50,897
Happened where's he?

302
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:53,717
Show Joker seems they survived

303
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:54,630
though I can't

304
00:19:54,713 --> 00:20:01,117
say how the.

305
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:05,437
Only thing left are the spots
they're standing on is this?

306
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:06,350
How the Navy acts.

307
00:20:06,433 --> 00:20:08,337
Now show some restraint—are you insane?

308
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:11,917
Even a blind man won't miss
with an attack that big!

309
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,157
Ah, pardon me now!

310
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:19,537
Law, you're a criminal; therefore,
I'll be arresting you now. I

311
00:20:19,620 --> 00:20:26,620
was

312
00:20:27,220 --> 00:20:31,397
falling

313
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:32,797
in love.

314
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:35,437
Oh ain't that sweet?

315
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:39,637
Oh hey, I think I can find the
factory—easy for real, yep.

316
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:42,237
Problem is we can't just wreck it.

317
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:44,457
wreck it Get the whole ass out of here.

318
00:20:44,540 --> 00:20:46,187
It's gonna be a whole thing.

319
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:47,439
A whole big thing.

320
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,560
Hey, you filthy little thief!

321
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:52,660
I told you we don't take credit!

322
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:54,480
Somebody stop that toy!

323
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:57,200
He took my burgers and didn't pay!

324
00:21:00,580 --> 00:21:03,227
We'll be lucky just to
make it out alive now.

325
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:05,640
Yeah, I heard about Doflamingo's trap.

326
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:07,757
Man, we walked right into that one.

327
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:09,977
But just cause our fancy
plan went off the rails

328
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:12,317
doesn't mean we can't do some
damage while we're in town.

329
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:15,797
I got something brewing here that
might salvage this operation.

330
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:17,137
Yeah, it's complicated.

331
00:21:17,220 --> 00:21:19,677
Just meet me at the flower
field and we'll work things out.

332
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:21,477
What the hell is that place anyway?

333
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:23,437
It sounds like something
out of a fairy tale.

334
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:27,620
By the way, I'm getting
worried about Nami. Come on.

335
00:21:27,980 --> 00:21:29,274
Nami's tough as nails.

336
00:21:29,360 --> 00:21:30,242
She'll be fine.

337
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:31,461
Have some faith.

338
00:21:32,740 --> 00:21:35,858
Besides, she got broken
monster chopper with her too.

339
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:38,980
Uh, something up?

340
00:21:41,360 --> 00:21:42,897
What are they watching there?

341
00:21:42,980 --> 00:21:43,810
That's green.

342
00:21:43,893 --> 00:21:45,637
They broadcast from the Coliseum.

343
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:48,757
The newcomer Luffy is putting
on a spoiler show today!

344
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:49,880
Love that beard!

345
00:21:50,040 --> 00:21:51,334
He's small, but quick!

346
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:58,440
Franky, I found Luffy, and he's, uh...

347
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:01,117
Yeah, he's fighting in
some big tournament.

348
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:02,517
I forgot to tell you that.

349
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:04,537
Why didn't you do anything to stop him?

350
00:22:04,620 --> 00:22:06,197
You can't trust him on his own!

351
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:08,574
Hey, you're in no position to judge me.

352
00:22:09,180 --> 00:22:11,298
Blackleg, I have to get out of here.

353
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:12,637
They're coming for me.

354
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:13,550
My men.

355
00:22:13,680 --> 00:22:17,297
You and your crew are trying to get
to Doflamingo's secret factory, right?

356
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:18,210
I have a map.

357
00:22:18,293 --> 00:22:19,260
It's disguised.

358
00:22:19,420 --> 00:22:21,577
It looks like a toy house on the exterior.

359
00:22:21,660 --> 00:22:23,013
But that's your target.

360
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:25,040
No, you can't.

361
00:22:25,300 --> 00:22:28,241
If you help me this much,
there's no turning back.

362
00:22:29,880 --> 00:22:31,820
It's too late. I'm doomed.

363
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:36,380
It seems the executives already
know that I betrayed the family.

364
00:22:41,040 --> 00:22:41,957
Violet, listen.

365
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:43,380
The Western Harbor.

366
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:45,014
You can meet me there.

367
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:47,341
Just stay hidden and wait for me.

368
00:22:47,620 --> 00:22:49,679
That's our cruise rendezvous point.

369
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:57,620
I swear, I'll get you out, no
matter what the cost may be.

370
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:00,310
Hopeless.

371
00:23:00,460 --> 00:23:01,695
You're just hopeless.

372
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:10,220
Pardon me, sir! Please fight!

373
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:11,539
Don't be hopeless!

374
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:13,195
Way to ruin the mood!

375
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:14,574
Where'd you come from?

376
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:15,560
Violet, wait!

377
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:18,460
Hurry! Defeat them!

378
00:23:19,560 --> 00:23:20,480
Don't move!

379
00:23:27,780 --> 00:23:28,610
Amazing!

380
00:23:28,693 --> 00:23:30,960
They're just thugs. Why'd you need me?

381
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:35,731
They are holding my dear friend Congeno
hostage, so I was rendered helpless.

382
00:23:36,340 --> 00:23:38,917
Speaking of which, I am
in dire need of your aid.

383
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,917
We must make haste to the toy house.

384
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:44,577
I have heard word that this is where
the fiends are holding Congeno,

385
00:23:44,660 --> 00:23:46,240
but I don't know the way.

386
00:23:56,500 --> 00:23:58,500
What the heck's going on up there?

387
00:23:59,940 --> 00:24:01,280
It must be long.

388
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,240
This sucks!

389
00:24:04,380 --> 00:24:06,697
If the roof caves in, then
we're all going to die!

390
00:24:06,780 --> 00:24:07,610
Whoa!

391
00:24:07,693 --> 00:24:09,140
Even the hero is scared now?

392
00:24:12,980 --> 00:24:13,810
Kidding?

393
00:24:13,893 --> 00:24:15,681
That earthquake was caused by me.

394
00:24:16,180 --> 00:24:17,700
Or my Haki?

395
00:24:18,360 --> 00:24:19,190
Haki?

396
00:24:19,273 --> 00:24:23,577
That's how you beat up all 50 ,000 of those
bad guys back on Fishman Island, right?

397
00:24:23,660 --> 00:24:24,490
So awesome!

398
00:24:24,680 --> 00:24:25,640
That's our hero!

399
00:24:27,300 --> 00:24:30,017
You're so strong, you can
shake the whole kingdom, huh?

400
00:24:30,100 --> 00:24:31,240
Try this, hero!

401
00:24:31,480 --> 00:24:32,480
A delicious gift!

402
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:34,500
A big piece of fighting fish!

403
00:24:34,620 --> 00:24:36,720
They're like goldfish, only angry!

404
00:24:37,040 --> 00:24:38,580
Those big guys? Yep!

405
00:24:41,620 --> 00:24:42,450
Wow!

406
00:24:42,700 --> 00:24:44,137
Didn't think it'd be so good!

407
00:24:44,220 --> 00:24:48,740
It's almost as tasty as Sea King, which
I dine on all the time, of course.

408
00:24:49,980 --> 00:24:50,860
I see.

409
00:24:51,280 --> 00:24:54,692
So they're the ones who nab
that thing back on the bridge.

410
00:24:55,300 --> 00:24:57,594
These little guys must be crazy strong.

411
00:24:57,880 --> 00:24:59,292
Glad they're on my side.

412
00:24:59,400 --> 00:25:00,297
Since we're small,

413
00:25:00,380 --> 00:25:01,977
just one of those fighting fish could feed

414
00:25:02,060 --> 00:25:04,177
the whole kingdom for
a month or even more.

415
00:25:04,260 --> 00:25:06,497
You big people have to
eat an awful lot, though.

416
00:25:06,580 --> 00:25:08,639
That must be a real pain sometimes.

417
00:25:08,860 --> 00:25:09,690
Huh?

418
00:25:10,340 --> 00:25:16,040
For Lufilon and my Ushalon fighting
force, a fish like this as just a snack.

419
00:25:17,940 --> 00:25:19,200
What's Usaland?

420
00:25:19,520 --> 00:25:20,480
That statue.

421
00:25:20,680 --> 00:25:21,920
Look familiar to ya?

422
00:25:25,620 --> 00:25:28,540
From that picture book
we read back in Jaya.

423
00:25:34,140 --> 00:25:37,500
Leo, is that... Noland? Uh-huh.

424
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:41,337
I see, of course.

425
00:25:41,420 --> 00:25:42,832
You know him, don't you?

426
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:47,980
He was the big person botanist who came
to visit our kingdom 400 years ago.

427
00:25:48,220 --> 00:25:49,050
Our hero!

428
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:52,657
Back then, there were a bunch
of bad guys messing up our home,

429
00:25:52,740 --> 00:25:56,497
but Noland rushed to the aid of
our ancestors and saved the day!

430
00:25:56,580 --> 00:26:00,837
We'll never forget the debt we owe to
Noland, no matter how many years pass.

431
00:26:00,920 --> 00:26:02,980
The Tumtada will always honor him!

432
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:08,297
When Ursuline mentioned the hero's name
and told us he was one of his descendants,

433
00:26:08,380 --> 00:26:09,210
I just...

434
00:26:09,293 --> 00:26:13,440
I was so overwhelmed! No! I
mean it! Look at my helmet!

435
00:26:13,720 --> 00:26:17,480
It's shaped like a chestnut,
just like his head! He's right!

436
00:26:17,780 --> 00:26:18,940
A chestnut head!

437
00:26:19,260 --> 00:26:21,360
We tied you up! It's awful!

438
00:26:21,520 --> 00:26:23,620
I am so sorry! You're shameless.

439
00:26:24,240 --> 00:26:26,260
Don't complain, it saved you too!

440
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:31,384
Just keep quiet, enjoy the feast,
and then we'll get out of here.

441
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:34,577
Truly, it must be an act of
fate that brought you here.

442
00:26:34,660 --> 00:26:35,860
And today, no less.

443
00:26:37,640 --> 00:26:38,840
Yes, I agree.

444
00:26:39,060 --> 00:26:44,080
After 400 long years have passed, a
legendary hero comes before us once again.

445
00:26:44,240 --> 00:26:47,887
on the very day that we vowed
to go to war against Doflamingo!

446
00:26:49,760 --> 00:26:50,590
Lucelyn,

447
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:51,677
after you finish eating,

448
00:26:51,760 --> 00:26:55,117
we'll take the underground passage
to the flower field and prepare.

449
00:26:55,200 --> 00:26:56,420
Now's the time!

450
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:03,817
The captain and his Rick royal army
are waiting for us in Dressrosa,

451
00:27:03,900 --> 00:27:06,700
where the final battle
will be waged. Yeah!

452
00:27:08,080 --> 00:27:09,840
Please, take the lead.

453
00:27:10,240 --> 00:27:11,780
Usher us to freedom!

454
00:27:12,320 --> 00:27:16,080
Together, we'll crush the
Don Quixote family! Yeah!

455
00:27:17,940 --> 00:27:20,060
With Usaland, we're invincible!

456
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:21,510
Yeah!

457
00:27:21,840 --> 00:27:23,360
Give him a cheer!

458
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:33,037
Usaland, yeah!
